      "dom_id": "question-51499",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "What is the root of the function $f(x)=\\frac{2x}{5}-3?$",
      "worked_solution": "The roots are the solutions to the equation $f(x)=0,$ which we solve as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{5}-3 & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{5} & =3 \\\\ 2x & =15 \\\\ x & =\\frac{15}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function has the single root $x=\\frac{15}{2}.$",
